{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-3-6-exist","title":"lem:dc-ch2-3-6-exist","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections.md","line":292,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections.tex#lem:dc-ch2-3-6-exist","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#def:dc-ch2-2-1]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#def:dc-ch2-3-4]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-3-6-koszul]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-3-6-welldef]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-tangent-extension]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections.tex","label":"lem:dc-ch2-3-6-exist","line":573,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[the Koszul-dual connection is Levi-Civita]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch2-3-6-exist}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch2-2-1, def:dc-ch2-3-4, lem:dc-ch2-3-6-koszul, lem:dc-ch2-3-6-welldef, lem:dc-ch2-tangent-extension}\n\n  \\dcref{ch2:3.6}\n  On a finite-dimensional, $\\sigma$-compact, Hausdorff Riemannian manifold,\n  suppose an affine connection satisfies\n  \\[\n    2\\langle\\nabla_YX,Z\\rangle=F_{Y,X}(Z)\n  \\]\n  for every $X,Y,Z$. Then it is symmetric and metric-compatible.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch2-3-6-koszul, lem:dc-ch2-tangent-extension}\n  \\sketch\n  The identities\n  \\[\n    F_{Y,X}(Z)-F_{X,Y}(Z)=2\\langle[X,Y],Z\\rangle\n  \\]\n  and\n  \\[\n    F_{Y,X}(Z)+F_{Z,X}(Y)=2X\\langle Y,Z\\rangle\n  \\]\n  follow by cancellation. The first, together with\n  \\cref{lem:dc-ch2-tangent-extension} and nondegeneracy, gives\n  $\\nabla_XY-\\nabla_YX=[X,Y]$. The second gives the product rule (4), hence\n  metric compatibility.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[the Koszul-dual connection is Levi-Civita] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368322d332d362d6578697374\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections%23def%3Adc-ch2-2-1\">↗ def:dc-ch2-2-1</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections%23def%3Adc-ch2-3-4\">↗ def:dc-ch2-3-4</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections%23lem%3Adc-ch2-3-6-koszul\">↗ lem:dc-ch2-3-6-koszul</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections%23lem%3Adc-ch2-3-6-welldef\">↗ lem:dc-ch2-3-6-welldef</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections%23lem%3Adc-ch2-tangent-extension\">↗ lem:dc-ch2-tangent-extension</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:3.6</span></span>On a finite-dimensional, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\sigma $\">$\\sigma $</span>-compact, Hausdorff Riemannian manifold, suppose an affine connection satisfies <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  2\\langle \\nabla _YX,Z\\rangle =F_{Y,X}(Z)  \\]\">\\[  2\\langle \\nabla _YX,Z\\rangle =F_{Y,X}(Z)  \\]</span> for every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$X,Y,Z$\">$X,Y,Z$</span>. Then it is symmetric and metric-compatible.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections%23lem%3Adc-ch2-3-6-koszul\">↗ lem:dc-ch2-3-6-koszul</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections%23lem%3Adc-ch2-tangent-extension\">↗ lem:dc-ch2-tangent-extension</a> \\sketch The identities </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  F_{Y,X}(Z)-F_{X,Y}(Z)=2\\langle [X,Y],Z\\rangle  \\]\">\\[  F_{Y,X}(Z)-F_{X,Y}(Z)=2\\langle [X,Y],Z\\rangle  \\]</span></p><p> and </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  F_{Y,X}(Z)+F_{Z,X}(Y)=2X\\langle Y,Z\\rangle  \\]\">\\[  F_{Y,X}(Z)+F_{Z,X}(Y)=2X\\langle Y,Z\\rangle  \\]</span></p><p> follow by cancellation. The first, together with <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections%23lem%3Adc-ch2-tangent-extension\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-tangent-extension\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368322d74616e67656e742d657874656e73696f6e\">section 2</a> and nondegeneracy, gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla _XY-\\nabla _YX=[X,Y]$\">$\\nabla _XY-\\nabla _YX=[X,Y]$</span>. The second gives the product rule (4), hence metric compatibility. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-3-6-affine","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#thm:dc-ch2-3-6","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#def:dc-ch2-2-1","title":"def:dc-ch2-2-1","label":"def:dc-ch2-2-1"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#def:dc-ch2-3-4","title":"def:dc-ch2-3-4","label":"def:dc-ch2-3-4"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-3-6-koszul","title":"lem:dc-ch2-3-6-koszul","label":"lem:dc-ch2-3-6-koszul"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-3-6-welldef","title":"lem:dc-ch2-3-6-welldef","label":"lem:dc-ch2-3-6-welldef"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-tangent-extension","title":"lem:dc-ch2-tangent-extension","label":"lem:dc-ch2-tangent-extension"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#thm:dc-ch2-3-6","title":"thm:dc-ch2-3-6","label":"thm:dc-ch2-3-6"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-3-6-exist","title":"lem:dc-ch2-3-6-exist","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[the Koszul-dual connection is Levi-Civita]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch2-3-6-exist}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch2-2-1, def:dc-ch2-3-4, lem:dc-ch2-3-6-koszul, lem:dc-ch2-3-6-welldef, lem:dc-ch2-tangent-extension}\n\n  \\dcref{ch2:3.6}\n  On a finite-dimensional, $\\sigma$-compact, Hausdorff Riemannian manifold,\n  suppose an affine connection satisfies\n  \\[\n    2\\langle\\nabla_YX,Z\\rangle=F_{Y,X}(Z)\n  \\]\n  for every $X,Y,Z$. Then it is symmetric and metric-compatible.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch2-3-6-koszul, lem:dc-ch2-tangent-extension}\n  \\sketch\n  The identities\n  \\[\n    F_{Y,X}(Z)-F_{X,Y}(Z)=2\\langle[X,Y],Z\\rangle\n  \\]\n  and\n  \\[\n    F_{Y,X}(Z)+F_{Z,X}(Y)=2X\\langle Y,Z\\rangle\n  \\]\n  follow by cancellation. The first, together with\n  \\cref{lem:dc-ch2-tangent-extension} and nondegeneracy, gives\n  $\\nabla_XY-\\nabla_YX=[X,Y]$. The second gives the product rule (4), hence\n  metric compatibility.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#def:dc-ch2-2-1","title":"def:dc-ch2-2-1","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#def:dc-ch2-3-4","title":"def:dc-ch2-3-4","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-3-6-koszul","title":"lem:dc-ch2-3-6-koszul","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-3-6-welldef","title":"lem:dc-ch2-3-6-welldef","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-tangent-extension","title":"lem:dc-ch2-tangent-extension","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}